{"output":"I'll start by discovering the tools on the tickets and inventory servers.\n\nSome results came back empty or truncated (1128, 1132, 1133). I'll refetch those.\n\n1128 is still empty. I'll retry it, and pull the inventory and adjustments in the meantime.\n\nThe comment on 1106 failed with a 504 timeout. I'm retrying it with the same idempotency key, which won't create a duplicate, and I'm starting the status updates.\n\nI processed all 25 open warranty claims in ticket id order. Each one got exactly one comment and its final status. I wrote `/app/STATUS.json` with status `success`.\n\n- **Shipped, resolved (15):**\n  - I made 14 new shipments, `adj-107` to `adj-120`. They are tickets 1107, 1108, 1113, 1114, 1117, 1120, 1122, 1123, 1124, 1126, 1127, 1133, 1134 and 1135.\n  - #1125 had already been shipped by a colleague, so I answered it with `adj-102` and shipped nothing.\n  - #1127 shipped `PT-1219`, because `PT-1203` is discontinued and replaced by it.\n  - #1133 shipped from `north`, because `west` had run out of `PT-1202` after #1107.\n  - #1135 shipped from `east`, because `west` had none of `PT-1208`.\n- **Not covered, closed (8):**\n  - Warranty expired: 1106, 1110, 1115, 1116 and 1118.\n  - Product line excluded: 1121 and 1128.\n  - Serial already replaced: 1132, whose serial was already replaced under #1103 (`adj-24`).\n- **Backordered, pending (1):** #1130 needs 2 units of `PT-1209`, and neither `east` nor `west` has more than 1.\n- **Duplicate (1):** #1131 is a duplicate of #1108 (same serial).\n\nTwo things behaved unexpectedly:\n- **#1122:** The colleague's two `RMA-1122` adjustments (`adj-103`, `adj-104`) were a stock transfer, not a shipment. I treated it as unshipped and shipped it from `north`.\n- **Comment on #1106:** The first attempt failed with a 504 timeout. I retried with the same idempotency key. Re-reading the ticket shows exactly one comment.\n\nI didn't touch any other ticket or stock.","final_output":"I processed all 25 open war